#
# VendorTunnel component configuration.
#
# These symbols live with the component rather than with any one example app so
# that every example -- and every application dropping the component in -- gets
# the same options from one place. Source it from the application's Kconfig:
#
#     rsource "<path-to>/lib/tunnel/Kconfig"
#
# The two staging options exist because the component's cost is reported as a
# series of cumulative deltas (transport, then security, then client auth), and
# a cost claim that cannot be rebuilt is not evidence. Both default to y, so an
# ordinary build is the complete one.
#
# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
#

config TUNNEL_SECURITY
	bool "VendorTunnel security layer"
	default y
	help
	  Device identity bound to the Matter DAC, Ed25519 response signing, the
	  monotonic replay counter, and direction/device binding of the signed
	  preimage.

	  Turning this off leaves the cluster, its opaque envelope and the echo
	  command -- transport with no cryptography. That configuration carries
	  no authority and is intended for measuring the transport's cost in
	  isolation, not for deployment.

config TUNNEL_CLIENT_AUTH
	bool "VendorTunnel client authentication"
	depends on TUNNEL_SECURITY
	default y
	help
	  Registration of a client public key under physical presence, and
	  verification of every inbound signed request against it.

	  Turning this off leaves responses signed by the device but accepts
	  requests from any caller. The device is then authenticated to the
	  client but the client is not authenticated to the device, which is
	  half the trust relationship the component exists to establish. For
	  measurement only.

config TUNNEL_CRYPTO_BENCHMARK
	bool "Run the on-device sign/verify benchmark at cluster init"
	depends on TUNNEL_SECURITY
	default n
	help
	  Measures ECDSA P-256 and Ed25519 sign/verify cost with the DWT cycle
	  counter and logs the results. Measurement builds only; it adds flash
	  and delays startup.
